# Paths in this directory that Mintlify must not publish. Mintlify builds every
# .md and .mdx file under docs/, including files that docs.json never lists.

# Archived CHANGELOG sections. The release-notes pages under source/ are the
# published history; this is the repository record.
/changelog/

# Contributor material. These were live on docs.lagerdata.com -- /STYLE,
# /TRANSLATION, /reference/gateway-auth-contract and /reference/net-9000-coverage
# all returned 200 -- because being absent from docs.json removes a page from
# the navigation, not from the build. They are working notes for people
# editing this repository, they carry relative paths that only resolve on
# GitHub, and they are outside the broken-links gate for that reason.
# Every rule here is anchored with a leading slash, which is what keeps it to
# this directory. An unanchored `reference/` also matches
# docs/source/reference/ -- the published CLI, Python, Rust and MCP reference
# -- and silently unpublishes a few hundred pages. `mint broken-links` caught
# exactly that: 54 broken links across 20 pages.
/STYLE.md
/TRANSLATION.md
/reference/
